Hooks in main.c. The version and flavor the build passes, and the engine list, feed the
banner and usage. The socket headers the resident code needs. The globals make's other
files and amk's modules share, among them make's own bsd_signal. The star and question
mark join the function-name characters. Usage lists amk's flags. Ahead of option decoding,
main settles the profile flag, the multi-call names and engine flags, --ape-list,
--ape-unpack, --bundle, the payload's tools and boot, and the resident roles. The feature
list, the engines and their versions, and the bindings ledgers become variables. The call
channel opens and the engines' init chunks run before the makefiles are read. The goal
references settle before the dependencies are snapped. A re-exec keeps the serve words. The
__main__ target can take the default goal. A zygote parks instead of running goals. Every
hook hears the goal list. The version banner names amk. The served child's side, which
adopts a request and runs it, and the goal list a spawned job runs, stay here, since they
use make's own goal state. die takes a guest's exit status, sweeps the spawned jobs, writes
the profile, and answers a served request.

